diagnosis_text:
Affected component: router4’s uplink interface to the core (eth5 on 172.25.1.0/24), not router3. Mechanism: PCs in Location C (192.168.200.0/24) use router4 (192.168.200.1) as default gateway. With router4’s upstream link down, router4 has no route toward Location A (172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24), so it immediately returns ICMP net-unreachable to the PCs.

Localization and evidence:
